  "content": {
    "id": "p11-q13-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "13",
    "prompt": "One side of a rectangle increases by 20% and the other side increases by 30%. Find the percentage increase in the area of the rectangle.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$56\\%$ increase.\n\nMultiply the side-length multipliers to find the area multiplier.",
      "worked": "Let the original side lengths be $l$ and $w$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}A_{\\text{original}} &= lw\\\\A_{\\text{new}} &= (1.2l)(1.3w)\\\\A_{\\text{new}} &= 1.56lw\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe new area is $156\\%$ of the original area, so the percentage increase is $156\\%-100\\%=56\\%$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 52
  },
